  "notes": "2 mono and 3 stereo channels, 3-band EQ, +48 V phantom power, MONITOR OUT and FX SEND (from the panel drawing and controls description). Each mono channel has MIC and LINE IN, but only one can be used at a time. USB (type B, stereo in/out) plays on the last stereo channel until a jack is plugged in there. MAIN OUT is impedance-balanced 6.35 mm TRS, PHONES unbalanced TRS, STREAM IN/OUT are RCA. Routing lists where a signal can go; knobs and STREAM buttons decide what actually reaches an output. DC power input not listed. Controls from the Quick Start Guide, 'Step 2: Controls': mono channels with GAIN, 3-band EQ (+/-15 dB), FX send, PAN and LEVEL; stereo channels with FX, BAL and LEVEL; STREAM TO MIX (STREAM input = RCA plus USB audio to the main mix), STREAM TO MONITOR/PHONES, PHANTOM (+48 V on all mono XLR inputs), PHONES/MONITOR level and MAIN MIX. As the guide states, USB audio plays on the last stereo channel (7/8) unless STREAM TO MIX is pressed or a jack is plugged into that channel. Band names (high, mid, low) as usual. Assumptions: the monitor/phones carry the main mix; the computer records the main mix; levels at MIN are silent.",
